{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788971256,"nonce":"XEgjPsekpEreGuHOcemNL87dbQY=","message":"SCOPING PASS, 2026-09-09. Read-only against decompiled 1.6 (`rimworld-tools/Info/decompiled/RimWorldBase/`), shipped defs, and `Source/AutoRimmer/`. No bench was touched, nothing built.\n\nThe premise is right and the p1 is right: 36 shipped `ThingDef`s carry `CompProperties_Usable`, plus 12 generated `Neurotrainer_*` and 29 generated `Psytrainer_*` — ~77 usable things at runtime on this bench's DLC set, and the verb surface reaches none of them. But **almost every specific citation in the body is wrong**, two acceptance bullets are unsatisfiable as written, the route contains a modal no shipped verb can answer, and there is an open issue that already owns half of this.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTIONS\n=====================================================================\n\n**1. `CanBeUsedBy` has no `out string failReason` — at either level.**\n`RimWorld/CompUsable.cs`: `public virtual AcceptanceReport CanBeUsedBy(Pawn p, bool forced = false, bool ignoreReserveAndReachable = false)`. One method, no overloads.\n`RimWorld/CompUseEffect.cs`: `public virtual AcceptanceReport CanBeUsedBy(Pawn p)`. One parameter.\nThe refusal string is `AcceptanceReport.Reason`, and **two clauses return a bare `false` with no reason at all** (see addition F).\n\n**2. \"`CompUseEffect.CanBeUsedBy` on each effect comp is the second half\" — no, it is the last clause of the first half.**\n`CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy` ends by walking `parent.AllComps` and calling `compUseEffect.CanBeUsedBy(p)` on each, returning the **first** non-accepted report. So one call already covers both. The consequence the spec should carry instead: **because it short-circuits, a verb that wants to publish every refusal must run the per-comp loop itself** — which `use-options` (see the boundary section) should, and the act path should not.\n\n**3. `CompUseEffect_FinishResearchProject` does not exist.** The class is **`CompUseEffect_FinishRandomResearchProject`**, and its gate is one line:\n```\nif (Find.ResearchManager.GetProject() == null) return \"NoActiveResearchProjectToFinish\".Translate();\n```\nIts `DoEffect` calls `FinishInstantly(project, usedBy)` → `Find.ResearchManager.FinishProject(proj, doCompletionDialog: true)`. See addition M — that `true` is a wedge.\n\n**4. \"`CompUseEffect_LearnSkill` refuses a pawn whose skill is already maxed or whose passion/incapability blocks it\" is FALSE, and one acceptance bullet depends on it.**\n```\npublic override AcceptanceReport CanBeUsedBy(Pawn p)\n{\n    if (p.skills == null) return false;\n    if (p.skills.GetSkill(Props.skill).TotallyDisabled) return \"SkillDisabled\".Translate();\n    return base.CanBeUsedBy(p);\n}\n```\nNo level check, no passion check. A level-20 pawn CAN use a neurotrainer; `DoEffect` is `user.skills.Learn(Props.skill, Props.xpGainAmount, direct: true)` and the XP is simply wasted. **\"maxed skill for a trainer\" is not a reachable refusal and must come out of the acceptance.** The two real ones are `p.skills == null` (a mech, an animal) and `TotallyDisabled` (backstory-disabled). Also: `Props.xpGainAmount` defaults to 50000f — the acceptance should say \"gains 50,000 XP in that skill\", not \"gains the skill levels\", because whether a level boundary is crossed depends on where the pawn started.\n\n**5. \"The right job is `JobDefOf.UseItem`, not `Ingest`\" is wrong twice.**\nThere is **no `JobDefOf.UseItem` field** — `RimWorld/JobDefOf.cs` has `UseNeurotrainer`, `UseVerbOnThing`, `UseCommsConsole`, `UseOutfitStand`, `UseStylingStation`, `GetNeuralSupercharge`, and no `UseItem`. The XML `JobDef UseItem` exists and would need `DefDatabase\u003cJobDef\u003e.GetNamed(\"UseItem\")`.\nAnd the job is **never hardcoded**: `TryStartUseJob` does `JobMaker.MakeJob(Props.useJob, parent)`. Shipped values of `useJob` are `UseItem`, `UseNeurotrainer`, `UseArtifact`, `InstallMechlink`, `TriggerObject`, `ReadDatacore`, `SmashThing` — **and `Ingest`**, on the four Anomaly serums (`JuggernautSerum`, `MetalbloodSerum`, `MindNumbSerum`, `VoidsightSerum`), which carry an `\u003cingestible\u003e` block AND `CompProperties_Usable`, with `showIngestFloatOption=false` so the player only ever sees \"Use\". Their `CompUsable.UsedBy` is invoked from `IngestionOutcomeDoer_UseThing.DoIngestionOutcomeSpecial`. **Read `Props.useJob`; never name a job def.**\n\n**6. `Neurotrainer_*` are not XML defs, and neither are the psytrainers.**\n`RimWorld/ThingDefGenerator_Neurotrainer.cs` builds all 41 in code: one `Neurotrainer_\u003cSkillDef\u003e` per `SkillDef` (**12**, correct) and one `Psytrainer_\u003cAbilityDef\u003e` per `AbilityDef` where `IsPsycast` (**29**, correct). `grep '\u003cdefName\u003eNeurotrainer' Data/` returns only `ThingCategoryDef`s. A worker that greps XML for these will find nothing and conclude they do not exist.\n\n**7. \"`MechSerumHealer`, `MechSerumResurrector`, psytrainers — same comp\" — three different comps, and one of the three is already reachable.**\n  * `MechSerumHealer` → `CompUseEffect_FixWorstHealthCondition`, refusing on `!HealthUtility.TryGetWorstHealthCondition(p, …)`. **And it is already reachable today**: `Items_Exotic.xml` also defines `RecipeDef AdministerMechSerumHealer` with `workerClass Recipe_AdministerUsableItem` on `Races_Humanlike.xml`, so `surgery-options` / `surgery-add` already surface it (git-bug `826d4bf` comment #1 established this).\n  * `MechSerumResurrector` → `CompTargetable_SingleCorpse` + `CompTargetEffect_Resurrect`. **This is `826d4bf`'s issue, not this one** — see the boundary section.\n  * Psytrainers → **`CompUseEffect_GainAbility`** (not `LearnAbility`), refusing on no `PsychicAmplifier` hediff and on already-known ability. Psylink level too low is only a `ConfirmMessage`, not a gate.\n\n**8. Comment #1's scope correction is RIGHT and understated, but its example is the wrong boss.**\n\"every `CompUsable`, buildings included\" — correct: `CommsConsole`, `FirefoamPopper`, `MechbandDish`, `BurnoutMechlinkBooster` are all `CompUsable` buildings. But `MechbandDish` is the caller for **Apocriton alone**; Diabolus's caller is `CommsConsole` and Warqueen's is `BurnoutMechlinkBooster` (`CompProperties_Useable_CallBossgroup.bossgroupDef`, and `CallBossgroupUtility.GetBossgroupCaller` reverse-scans the DefDatabase for it). That does not weaken the point — it strengthens it: an ordinary comms console is a `CompUsable` building, so `use` scoped to items would miss the single most common building in the game.\nComment #1's other claims verify clean: `Mechlink` really is in `Biotech/Defs/HediffDefs/Hediffs_Mechanitor.xml`, `PsychicAmplifier` really is in `Core/Defs/HediffDefs/Hediffs_Psycasts.xml` (Core, `MayRequireAnyOf` Royalty/Biotech), and **neither has any surgery recipe** — no RecipeDef anywhere lists either as an ingredient or `addsHediff`. Both are use-only. Confirmed by grep over the whole `Data/` tree.\n\n**9. `queue` CANNOT be honoured through `TryStartUseJob`, so that acceptance bullet forces the implementation.**\n`StartJob()` ends `pawn.jobs.TryTakeOrderedJob(job, JobTag.Misc)` — no `requestQueueing` parameter, exactly the shape that made `attack` refuse `queue` with a gate (`PawnOrderVerbs.cs` header, git-bug `bc2250b`). \"`queue` is honoured the way `consume` honours it\" is satisfiable **only** if the verb reproduces `StartJob` and calls `PawnActs.TakeOrder(pawn, job, JobTag.Misc, queued, out eff)` itself. Which it must do anyway — see addition A.\n\n=====================================================================\nADDITIONS\n=====================================================================\n\n**A. THE BLOCKING ONE: `TryStartUseJob` RAISES A FORCE-PAUSING MODAL THAT NO SHIPPED VERB CAN ANSWER.**\n```\nforeach (CompUseEffect comp in parent.GetComps\u003cCompUseEffect\u003e())\n{ TaggedString ts = comp.ConfirmMessage(pawn); if (!ts.NullOrEmpty()) …append… }\nif (text.NullOrEmpty()) StartJob();\nelse Find.WindowStack.Add(Dialog_MessageBox.CreateConfirmation(text, StartJob));\n```\n`Verse/Dialog_MessageBox.cs` — `public class Dialog_MessageBox : Window`, `forcePause = true`. Per spec 1.7 every subsequent `advance` halts at 0 ticks with `reason:\"dialog\"`.\n**And 3.5 does not clear it.** `dialog-choose` (`DialogVerbs.cs`) takes a `Dialog_NodeTree` and reads `curNode.options`; `Dialog_MessageBox` is not a `Dialog_NodeTree` and has `buttonAAction`/`buttonBAction`, not `DiaOption`s. `dialog-accept` (`NameDialogs.cs`) answers text-entry naming windows only. `dialog-dismiss` would `TryRemove` the window — which **cancels** the confirmation, so the use never happens. There is no route to \"press Accept\".\nThree `ConfirmMessage` overriders: `CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup` (always non-empty — the wave roster), `CompUseEffect_InstallImplantMechlink` (when the pawn's Smithing work type or Intellectual work tag is disabled), `CompUseEffect_GainAbility` (psylink level below the psycast's).\n**And there is a SECOND, separate modal one level up.** `RimWorld/CompUsableImplant.cs` overrides `TryStartUseJob` entirely and raises its own `new Dialog_MessageBox(text, \"Yes\", …, \"No\")` from `CompRoyalImplant.CheckForViolations` before ever reaching `base.TryStartUseJob`. `CompUsableImplant` is the comp class on **`Mechlink`, `PsychicAmplifier`, and all six mechanitor implants** — i.e. on exactly the two defs comment #1 filed this as p1 for.\n**Ruling: `use` reproduces `StartJob` and never calls `TryStartUseJob`.** It pre-collects the `ConfirmMessage` set, transacts it as accepted, and DISCLOSES it on the result — the shipped `dialogs_skipped` pattern from `equip` (bladelink / persona-weapon) and `wear` (mechanitor bandwidth), and `MedicalBillVerbs`' `sendMessages:false`. `CompUsableImplant`'s royal-title violation text is re-derived the same way, from `CompRoyalImplant.CheckForViolations`, and published — a title violation is a real consequence the agent owes a decision on, so it is named, not swallowed.\n\n**B. `SelectedUseOption` short-circuits the whole route, and that is `826d4bf`'s half.** The float-menu action's first act is `foreach (CompUseEffect comp …) if (comp.SelectedUseOption(myPawn)) return;`. `RimWorld/CompTargetable.cs` is the only overrider: when `PlayerChoosesTarget` it sets `caster = p`, calls `Find.Targeter.BeginTargeting(this, …)` and returns true — **`TryStartUseJob` is never reached**. `use` must detect a `CompTargetable` on the parent and refuse with a named gate pointing at the targetable verb, rather than starting a job whose effect will silently no-op.\n\n**C. `CompUseableDatacore` is a third override the spec does not know about.** `RimWorld/CompUseableDatacore.cs : CompUsable` overrides `CanBeUsedBy` (adds `\"NoResearchBench\"` when `GetExtraTarget(p)` has no thing), overrides `GetExtraTarget` (nearest reachable research bench) and `UsedBy`; its job is `ReadDatacore` → `JobDriver_UseItemResearchBench`, which hauls the item to the bench. One shipped def: `MechanoidTransponder`. So `use` cannot assume `GetExtraTarget` is invalid, and must call the virtual rather than hardcoding `LocalTargetInfo.Invalid`.\n\n**D. The gate chain in full — the issue lists two of nine.** `CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy`, in order, each needing its own gate name:\n  1. `!p.RaceProps.IsFlesh` → **bare `false`, no reason**\n  2. `p.IsMutant \u0026\u0026 !Props.allowedMutants.Contains(p.mutant.Def)` → **bare `false`, no reason** (`allowedMutants: [Ghoul]` on the four Anomaly serums is the only shipped non-empty value)\n  3. `layerWhitelist` → `\"CannotPerformPlanetLayer\"`\n  4. `layerBlacklist` → `\"CannotPerformPlanetLayer\"`\n  5. `CompPowerTrader` present and `!PowerOn` → `\"NoPower\"` (reachable: `CommsConsole`)\n  6. `!p.CanReach(parent, PathEndMode.Touch, Danger.Deadly)` → `\"NoPath\"`\n  7. `!p.CanReserve(parent, 1, -1, null, forced)` → `\"ReservedBy\"` (naming the reserver, from `reservationManager.FirstRespectedReserver` ?? `physicalInteractionReservationManager.FirstReserverOf`) or `\"Reserved\"`\n  8. `Props.userMustHaveHediff` → `\"MustHaveHediff\"` — reachable on six shipped defs (`ControlSublink`, `ControlSublinkHigh`, `MechFormfeeder`, `RemoteRepairer`, `RemoteShielder`, `RepairProbe`), all requiring `MechlinkImplant`\n  9. each `CompUseEffect.CanBeUsedBy(p)`, first refusal wins\nIt uses `CanReach` and `CanReserve` **separately**, not `CanReserveAndReach`. `PawnActs.CanReachThing(pawn, thing, PathEndMode.Touch, out reason)` is the shipped helper for clause 6 and already spells the refusal as the game does.\n\n**E. Two clauses have NO reason string, and the verb must not print an empty one.** Clauses 1 and 2 above return `false`, so `AcceptanceReport.Reason` is `\"\"`. `PawnActs.Tr(key, fallback)` exists precisely so a phrase of ours is labelled as ours; use it, and give both their own gate (`not-flesh`, `mutant`).\n\n**F. `p.MapHeld.Tile` is dereferenced with no null guard** (clause 3's setup). Same shape as `PawnSafe` Class D (`Pawn_PlayerSettings.EffectiveAreaRestrictionInPawnCurrentMap`). A verb reproducing the clause must guard `MapHeld`.\n\n**G. What is NOT gated at the widget, and must therefore NOT be refused.**\n  * **Forbidden.** No `IsForbidden` check exists anywhere from the provider down to `TryStartUseJob`. The only forbidden gate is `FailOnDespawnedNullOrForbidden(TargetIndex.A)` on the job driver's wait toil. Follow `equip`/`wear`/`consume`: `thing.SetForbidden(false)` before ordering, in a try/catch, and say so on the line.\n  * **Drafted.** `FloatMenuOptionProvider_FromThing` sets `Drafted =\u003e true` and `Undrafted =\u003e true`. A drafted pawn may use.\n  * **Manipulation.** `RequiresManipulation =\u003e false` on the provider; the only check is `this.FailOnIncapable(PawnCapacityDefOf.Manipulation)` **inside** `JobDriver_UseItem`. So refusing a manipulation-incapable pawn up front would fabricate a restriction the player does not have — the `261f2e9` error facing the other way. **Publish it as an advisory** (`would_fail_on: manipulation`), citing the job driver, and let the order go.\n  * `MechanoidCanDo =\u003e false` on the provider IS a real gate — mechs get no option.\n  * `CanTargetDespawned =\u003e false` — the item must be `Spawned`. An item in an inventory or a container offers nothing. `PawnActs.ThingArg` already resolves only from `map.listerThings.AllThings`, so this is satisfied for free; say so rather than adding a check.\n\n**H. `CanBeUsedBy` runs FOUR times on a normal use, and the last two matter.** Float menu → `TryStartUseJob` → `JobDriver_UseItem.MakeNewToils`' `this.FailOn(() =\u003e !comp.CanBeUsedBy(pawn))` (evaluated continuously for the whole job) → `CompUsable.UsedBy` with `ignoreReserveAndReachable: true`. Consequence for the result: an accepted `use` can still die mid-job when a gate flips, and the job-driver `FailOn` uses `forced: false` regardless of what we passed. `OrderEffect`/`JobLine` already carry the right vocabulary for reporting the take; the acceptance should assert the EFFECT, not the acceptance of the order (the `4087644` rule).\n\n**I. `UsedBy` runs the effects in DESCENDING `OrderPriority`, and destruction is a comp, not a rule.** `CompUseEffect_DestroySelf.OrderPriority =\u003e Props.orderPriority`, default **-1000f**, so it is always last. \"the item is destroyed\" holds only for defs that carry `CompProperties_UseEffectDestroySelf` — the generated neurotrainers/psytrainers inherit it from the code-built `BaseNeurotrainer`, `TechprofSubpersonaCore` and `MechSerumHealer` declare it, `Mechlink` inherits it from `MechanitorImplantBase`. Assert per-def, not universally. Effects run inside a `try/catch` that `Log.Error`s — a modded comp that throws produces a RED ERROR on our path and the result should surface it rather than reporting a clean success.\n\n**J. THE TECHPROF CORE WEDGES THE RUN, AND THE ACCEPTANCE HAS TO SAY HOW TO UN-WEDGE IT.**\n`CompUseEffect_FinishRandomResearchProject.FinishInstantly` calls `Find.ResearchManager.FinishProject(proj, doCompletionDialog: true)`, and that flag runs\n`Find.WindowStack.Add(new Dialog_NodeTree(diaNode, delayInteractivity: true))`.\n`Verse/Dialog_NodeTree.cs` sets `forcePause = true; closeOnCancel = false;`. This fires at `DoEffect` time — i.e. **during the `advance` that runs the job**, not at order time — so the acceptance is: order the use, advance, the run halts with `reason:\"dialog\"`, and `dialog-choose` answers it (this one IS a `Dialog_NodeTree`, so 3.5 covers it). Write that into the acceptance or the bench check will read as a regression.\nAlso: `FinishProject` **recursively finishes unfinished prerequisites** and calls `AddTechprints` to satisfy techprint requirements. One core can finish a chain, not one project. And it ends `if (currentProj == proj) currentProj = null;` — so the acceptance's `current: null` is correct.\n\n**K. `showUseGizmo` is a second player route and is not reproducible headless.** `CompUsable.CompGetGizmosExtra` yields a `Command_Action` whose action is `Find.Targeter.BeginTargeting(this)`; `CompUsable` is itself an `ITargetingSource` and `OrderForceTarget` is where that lands. It is set on `TechprofSubpersonaCore`, `MechSerumHealer`, the neurotrainers/psytrainers and the Anomaly serums — but NOT on `Mechlink`, the six mechanitor implants, or any of the buildings. The float-menu route is the one to reproduce; name the gizmo route as the second player route we deliberately do not drive, with the reason (it arms `Find.Targeter` and consumes the next click).\n\n**L. The `not-usable` acceptance bullet needs its mirror in `consume`.** The bullet as written is right. Add: `PawnOrderVerbs.Consume`'s `not-ingestible` gate should name `use` — the four Anomaly serums set `showIngestFloatOption=false` and land in exactly that refusal today, correctly, with no onward pointer.\n\n=====================================================================\nSCOPE BOUNDARY — THIS ISSUE AND `826d4bf`\n=====================================================================\n**git-bug `826d4bf` (open, `wave:3`, p2, \"No verb can use a targetable item on a target\") already owns half of this verb**, and its comment #1 (2026-08-31 verification pass) independently found the same `Dialog_MessageBox` on `TryStartUseJob` and the private-field problem in `CompTargetable`. The two issues bottom out in the same `CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy` chain, the same `StartJob` reproduction, and the same modal decision.\n\n**Recommendation: do not build them in parallel, and do not merge them into one worker's spec either.** Instead:\n  * **`d318d4a` OWNS the shared route** — a `UsableSafe`-style helper reproducing all nine `CanBeUsedBy` clauses and `StartJob`, plus the `use {pawns, thing, queue?}` verb and a `use-options {pawn?, thing?}` read (the `surgery-options` shape: what the game would offer, whether it is clickable, and the game's own reason when not). Scope: `CompUsable`, `CompUsableImplant`, `CompUseableDatacore`, and every `CompUseEffect` that is not a `CompTargetable`.\n  * **`826d4bf` is reduced to a strict dependent**: add the `target` argument, seat `CompTargetable.selectedTarget`/`caster`, reproduce `CompTargetable.ValidateTarget` + `GetTargetingParameters().CanTarget`, and assert the corpse is gone. It should carry a `depends: d318d4a` note and lose the `CanBeUsedBy` half of its own scope.\nIf the orchestrator would rather have one issue, merging is defensible and cheaper — the argument against splitting is that two workers will otherwise write the same nine-clause gate chain in two files and they will diverge, which is the forked-catalogue failure `WorldSafe` exists to prevent. **Either way, `826d4bf` must not be dispatched before `d318d4a`.**\n\n`88880d7` (`bossgroup-call`) also bottoms out here; see my comment on that issue — the act is `use`, and `88880d7` keeps only the discovery half.\n\n=====================================================================\nSIZE AND DEPENDENCY\n=====================================================================\n**Dependency: none inbound.** This is the root of the batch — `826d4bf` and `88880d7` both depend on it. `eb35e1a` and `ae84a07` are independent of it.\n\n**Size: three files, ~700–900 lines.** A new `UsableSafe.cs` (or a section of `ThingVerbs.cs`) at ~250 for the reproduced chain, the `ConfirmMessage` pre-collection and `StartJob`; `PawnOrderVerbs.cs` +~250 for `use` and `use-options`; `PawnOrderVerbs.Consume` +~5 for the onward pointer in L.\n\n**The risky part is A — the modal.** Everything else is a faithful transcription of a chain that is fully readable. The modal is where a plausible implementation (`call TryStartUseJob, it is the game's own method`) produces a run that halts forever on a `Dialog_MessageBox` nothing can press, on the two defs this issue was filed for. That failure would appear only at bench acceptance, under `advance`, after the order reported `ok:true`.\n\n**Second risk: `Props.useJob` is per-def and one shipped value is `Ingest`.** A verb that assumes `JobDriver_UseItem` semantics — `useDuration`, the goto toil, the `FailOnIncapable` — is wrong for those four serums, where the ingest driver runs instead and `UsedBy` is called from an outcome doer.","files":null}]}